{"title":"2002 USA TST Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Titu Andreescu</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94bd9d7a26cd1112d46cfcebde46607448791e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle ABC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> be a triangle. Prove that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5fb735f5ba13a5e7ef90e6fc8b64d4ca7fd2f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\sin\\frac{3A}{2} + \\sin\\frac{3B}{2} + \\sin\\frac{3C}{2} \\le \\cos\\frac{A-B}{2} + \\cos\\frac{B-C}{2} + \\cos\\frac{C-A}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"520\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first note that \n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc5ed016a1a582f7ddc0c3dfd8bad3818ad4ddd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\frac{A-B}{2} = \\cos\\left( \\frac{\\pi - (2B + c)}{2} \\right) = \\sin\\frac{2B + C}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"377\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Hence the inequality becomes\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/611f3e397ce5414f3f38137a83deabf9aaa66d3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\frac{3A}{2} + \\sin\\frac{3B}{2} + \\sin\\frac{3C}{2} \\le \\sin\\frac{2A+B}{2} + \\sin\\frac{2B+C}{2} + \\sin\\frac{2C+A}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"536\" height=\"38\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>or\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3d2fe352de66cab96ef24063b6061484f6570e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{\\rm cyc} \\sin A \\cos A/2 + \\sum_{\\rm cyc} \\cos A \\sin A/2 \\le \\sum_{\\rm cyc} \\sin A \\cos B/2 + \\sum_{\\rm cyc} \\cos A \\sin B/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"589\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>We now note that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5d34ca397a7ca42a7d29fe0e311c5f486cd5721.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in [0, \\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/484155f1042126a0c94805e2bef1f5c7f2f5f4c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\cos x$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" /> is decreasing and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/4/d54884c7f8e2d3afe40c5f710186b6b7816bf1e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\sin x/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> is increasing.  It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c454d15306f7844de5712cbeb394620f8885ddc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\cos A, \\cos B, \\cos C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb905e30b117d0d4acb2f091809e6c09758e4f1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\sin A/2, \\sin B/2, \\sin C/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"18\" /> are sorted in opposing order, so by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rearrangement_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rearrangement inequality\">rearrangement inequality</a>,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65a30f0a18fcec155d3d7b47ce867a5380a1df4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{\\rm cyc} \\cos A \\sin A/2 \\le \\sum_{\\rm cyc} \\cos B \\sin B/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"285\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Now, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/758db4e8e3b1861a3f7d84059d31e9f97aa8a5f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in [0, \\pi/2 ]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aab51d17d30c7158712640f12da7809f5585bf05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> increases, and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5d34ca397a7ca42a7d29fe0e311c5f486cd5721.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in [0, \\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/402b658bfb53b656277b4c32d36e7b6f77a31e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\cos x/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> decreases; hence if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94bd9d7a26cd1112d46cfcebde46607448791e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle ABC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is an acute or right triangle, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154f8f666a89a0cf38cd5c9f7db6492648a60a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\sin A, \\sin B, \\sin C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/0424b514a2682a39a1cd76404374f0eb667c1cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\cos A/2, \\cos B/2, \\cos C/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" /> are oppositely sorted.  But if one angle, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734ef645c78704dbe5a136258a49d8425298f623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle A$\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" />, is obtuse, then we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a846289b2a24dfd8992614491a593413b0014409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin B, \\sin C \\le \\sin (B+C) = \\sin A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"265\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154f8f666a89a0cf38cd5c9f7db6492648a60a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\sin A, \\sin B, \\sin C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/0424b514a2682a39a1cd76404374f0eb667c1cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\cos A/2, \\cos B/2, \\cos C/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" /> will still be oppositely sorted, and again by the rearrangement inequality,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/131c42f7685e5b71454bc7cd680936699f7a819e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{\\rm cyc} \\sin A \\cos A/2 \\le \\sum_{\\rm cyc} \\sin A \\cos B/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"284\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Adding these two conditions yields the desired inequality.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USA_TST_Problems\" title=\"2002 USA TST Problems\">2002 USA TST Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=371474#p371474\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=3911\">More Discussion</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174001\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 131/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 356/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4863/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.012      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    6.012      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4832:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174001 and revision id 14344. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}